# Canonical-shape exceptions — Thoth
#
# Grammar (rules-library/platform/canonical-app-shape.md, enforced by
# check-canonical-shape.py):  <invariant-key>  <YYYY-MM-DD>  # reason
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT COVER
#
# canonical-app-shape.md opens "Every household full-stack app". Thoth is a
# Tauri desktop app: it has no backend package and no vertical api/<domain>/
# slices, and it never will, because there is no server. Those two invariants
# are STRUCTURAL CORE and the rule forbids excepting them from a repo-local
# file — correctly, since doing so would mint a new archetype by the back door.
#
# So `src-layout` and `domain-slices` are deliberately ABSENT below. They stay
# genuinely unsatisfied, and closing them needs a reviewed desktop-app clause in
# canonical-app-shape.md itself, not a line here. Raised against the household
# governance repo as poodle64/master-project#314, where Thoth and the estate's
# other Tauri app are the two reference consumers such a clause would have.
# It is an open question for the RULE, not drift this repo can resolve.
#
# What IS recorded below is the root inventory, which the rule requires per
# entry rather than wholesale. Every line is a divergence Thoth keeps on
# purpose; anything that could simply go has gone instead (RELEASING.md and
# .env.example were deleted on 2026-08-27 rather than excepted).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The SvelteKit app is the repo root.
#
# ONE structural fact, not sixteen decisions: the canonical template puts the
# frontend under frontend/, and a Tauri app's web layer IS the repo root —
# vite, svelte-kit and tauri all resolve it from there. Each entry below is the
# template's frontend/<name> sitting at <name> instead. Recorded per entry
# because the rule requires it; they stand or fall together.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
